{"author":{"id":"fb9734b7331903226ef3f5df545b960dd5ac64d18b49faee11e8b8e0bd561c91"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1783423926,"nonce":"X/Mi434m/kpEGmemeNQ0zr94qf4=","title":"Sampling rides the WDDM cliff: device_free=0.00 at peak in ingraph smoke","message":"Observed in all 4 A/B smoke runs on 2026-07-07 (scripts/smoke_krea2_ingraph_cuda.py\n--ab-eager, Krea2 mixed resident+ingraph sampling, RTX 4070 11.99 GiB):\n\n[MemoryManager] sampling peak: torch_allocated=9.70 GiB sampling_extra=3.58 GiB\nlearned_working_reserve=3.21 GiB (free fits ~0.0 more forwards);\ntorch_allocated=7.16 GiB torch_reserved=10.97 GiB\ndevice_used=11.99/11.99 GiB device_free=0.00 GiB\n\nThe card sits at the full dedicated ceiling during sampling -- past the ~11.5 GiB\nWDDM churn cliff -- so the OS silently pages GPU memory. No error is raised\n(dedicated-cliff failure mode), just nondeterministic slowdown.\n\nImpact: the compiled+streamed measured pass swings 0.79 / 1.34 / 1.68 / 1.60\ns/forward across otherwise-identical runs, while the eager baseline pass stays\nflat at ~1.45-1.49. Per-pass dynamo counters are identical between warmup and\nmeasured pass in every run, so recompilation is ruled out; the variance is\npaging pressure. This currently masks any real perf comparison of compile-path\nchanges.\n\nContributing factors to investigate:\n\n1. Reserve model says \"free fits ~0.0 more forwards\" and proceeds -- it\n   believes the budget exactly fits, yet device_free is 0. Likely the\n   allocated-side signal vs device-used mismatch: torch_reserved=10.97 GiB\n   while torch_allocated=7.16 GiB, i.e. ~3.4 GiB of caching-allocator slack\n   is pushing device_used to the ceiling but is invisible to an\n   allocated-side budget. Same failure shape as the training headroom\n   lesson: govern on (total-free) cohabitation watermark vs the cliff, not\n   on allocated.\n2. The A/B smoke passes skip_sampling_guard=True for both samples, so the\n   reactive cohabitation guard never streams a resident block back to\n   relieve pressure. Real training runs have the guard; the smoke does not.\n3. In A/B mode the eager baseline runs first inside the same\n   inference_resident context; its allocator footprint (reserved pool) is\n   inherited by the compiled passes. torch.cuda.empty_cache() runs between\n   warmup and measured pass but reserved still shows 10.57-10.97 GiB at peak.\n4. Retained ingraph layout (keep_ingraph_sampling) holds the 15 host packs\n   and compiled state alive across warmup+measured -- intended, but its\n   device-side cost should be visible to the reserve model.\n\nWhere: toolkit/memory_management/manager.py (inference_resident residency\nplanner / sampling working reserve / sampling guard). Numbers above from\n.codex/krea2_ingraph_cuda_smoke_ab*.json and the four task logs.\n\nAcceptance: sampling peak keeps device_free \u003e= the configured WDDM margin\n(default 1.0 GiB) in the ingraph A/B smoke, and measured-pass s/forward\nvariance collapses accordingly.","files":null}]}